    <string name="settings_when_full">when full</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_main_brush">Replace after about 300 hours of cleaning.\n\nOnce a week, take the brush out, cut away hair wound around it and clean the end caps. A worn brush leaves dust behind on carpets.</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_side_brush">Replace after about 200 hours of cleaning.\n\nOnce a month, pull it off and remove hair from around its base. Replace it sooner when the bristles are bent.</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_filter">Replace after about 150 hours of cleaning.\n\nOnce a week, tap the dust out of the filter over a bin. Rinse it only if it is a washable filter, and let it dry completely before putting it back.</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_sensor">Clean after about 30 hours of cleaning.\n\nWipe the cliff sensors underneath, the wall sensor, the charging contacts and the camera window with a soft dry cloth, then reset the counter.</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_maintenance_brush">Replace after about 300 hours.\n\nThis brush in the dock scrubs the mop wash tray. Rinse off hair and dirt when you clean the tray.</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_strainer">Clean when needed; the robot counts mop washes since the last reset.\n\nTake out the strainer in the dock\'s wash tray, rinse it under the tap and put it back.</string>
    <string name="settings_guide_dust_bag">Replace when it is full; the dock warns you.\n\nThe robot counts how often the dock emptied it since the last reset, which gives an idea of how full it is.</string>
